# Review this manuscript

A complete manuscript is at `/workspace/paper/`. Its toplevel TeX file is
`{{ main_tex }}`{% if pdf %}, and the compiled PDF is `{{ pdf }}`{% endif %}.
It is a {{ domain }} paper submitted to {{ venue }}.

Read it and write a peer review.

## What to produce

Write your review to **`/workspace/submission/review.md`**. That is the only
required output. Anything else you find useful — structured findings, per-section
notes, a scratch summary — is yours to decide, and will be archived alongside it
without affecting your assessment.

## What a review is expected to do here

Your review is assessed on whether it identifies the manuscript's genuine
defects: places where the paper claims more than it establishes, where an
argument has a gap, where a statement is not supported by what precedes it,
where attribution is wrong or missing, or where the presentation misleads a
reader about what was actually done.

Be specific. A finding that names a location and says what is wrong with it is
worth more than a general impression. Quote or point to the passage you mean.

Reporting problems that are not there is not free: a review that lists every
possible objection in the hope of covering the real ones scores worse than one
that reports what it can actually support.

If you are uncertain whether something is a defect, say so and say why, rather
than either suppressing it or asserting it.

## Ground rules

- `/workspace/paper/` is read-only input. Do not modify it.
- Judge the manuscript as submitted. Do not rewrite it.
{% if protocol == "offline" %}
- **You have no network access.** Assess the manuscript on its own terms, from
  what is on the page. Where a claim would need checking against outside
  literature you cannot reach, say that it needs checking rather than guessing
  at the answer.
{%- else %}
- **You have network access** to scholarly sources ({{ allowed_hosts | join(", ") }}).
  Checking the manuscript's claims and attributions against the literature is
  part of this task.
{%- endif %}
- Do not fabricate citations, quotations, or results.

## Working space

- `/workspace/submission/` — your review goes here.
- `/logs/agent/` — scratch space for your own run logs, archived with the trial.
- LaTeX (`pdflatex`, `latexmk`) and `poppler-utils` (`pdftotext`, `pdftoppm`) are
  installed if you want to compile the source or rasterise pages to inspect
  figures.
